# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MICHAEL ROW THE BOAT ASHORE (In G) – The Highwaymen/Peter, Paul & Mary
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
{ns}
{define: Bm base-fret 1 frets x 0 4 4 3 2} 
{define: Gadd base-fret 1 frets 3 2 0 0 3 3} 
{t: MICHAEL ROW THE BOAT ASHORE (In G) – Highwaymen/Peter, Paul & Mary}
{st: (Saletan/Traditional) }
{artist: The Highwaymen; Peter, Paul & Mary}
{composer:  Michael Saletan}


Two versions here, first for the Highwaymen, and afterwards one for Peter, Paul, & Mary which add some verses the Highwaymen do not. There's also a version in C.

TIP:  If transposing, play the root chord of the transposed (Gadd) adding the 5th note as necessary.

TIP:  If you want to get a little fancy and add some nice voicing which all involves simply lifting and replacing an existing finger:  (G) Michael (Gadd) row (lift off 2nd string/3rd fret) the (replace) boat (lift off 1st string) a (replace) shore, (lift off) hal (replace) le (C) lu (G) jah.  Michael row the (C) boat (lift off index finger) a (D) shore, halle (G) lu (D) u (G) jah.
 

